Description: GHSA-vc5h-9ppw-p5f3 (CVE-2026-7260): a tar archive with a loop of symbolic links no longer exhausts the stack (phar_get_link_source() follows the chain without recursion, with Floyd's cycle detection; a loop resolves to nothing). GHSA-j3wh-g957-2m85: tar entry injection: an entry size that is not plain octal (overflow, GNU base-256, other characters) is refused instead of being read as some other size, entries that carry no data (links, devices, directories, FIFOs) no longer skip data, GNU long link records are refused and a long name longer than the archive is rejected. The test of GHSA-vc5h writes its archives itself, as patch(1) cannot add the binary ones of upstream.
Origin: php-src commits 69821305b4c6 (03.05.2026) and f3432d2d2a01 (13.09.2026, both Jakub Zelenka) of the PHP 7.4 security branch of Remi Collet (remicollet/php-src-security PHP-7.4-security-backports), ported to the PHP 5 API

